{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>את פני הפרכת.</b> And above it says אֶת פְּנֵי פָרֹכֶת הַקֹּדֶשׁ — parable to a king against whom a province rebelled: if part of it rebelled, his retinue endures; if all of it rebelled, his retinue does not endure. So too here: when the anointed priest sinned, the name of the holiness of the Place was still upon the Sanctuary; once all of them sinned — perish the thought — the holiness departed (Zevachim 41a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:56.260968655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}